# Martini 3.0.0's own bonded force constants for proteins. Generated by
# data/martini3/prepare_martini3_data.py -- do not edit by hand. It is read
# only when -bondstiffness is given, alongside -rigidbody
# data/reducerules/martini3.rbody, whose springs it retunes.
#
# STIFFNESS <res> <a1> <a2> <k>, k in kJ.mol-1.A-2. TORSIONTABLE <id> <bins>
# <E_0> <T_0> ... over xi in [-180, 180], E in kJ/mol and T = -dV/dxi in
# kJ.mol-1.rad-1. TORSION <res> PLANARITY <a1> <a2> <a3> <a4> <table>.
#
# A STIFFNESS RECORD RETUNES AND CREATES NOTHING, so every record here names
# a pair that martini3.rbody already springs: 141 records over 141 of its 171
# groups, and not one record naming a pair with no spring. Of the 30 groups
# left, 26 are Martini [constraints] -- rigid, carrying NO force constant --
# and 4 are the pairs tying in tryptophan's SC3, which is Martini's massless
# virtual site and ours alone. Martini's "#ifdef FLEXIBLE" fallback of
# 1000000 kJ.mol-1.nm-2 is a workaround for engines without constraints, not
# a force-field value, so nothing is written for any of them: they keep the
# run's uniform -stiffness.
#
# Every number is converted out of GROMACS units here. A force constant in
# kJ.mol-1.nm-2 divided by 100 is kJ.mol-1.A-2, and both engines write a bond
# as 0.5 k (r - r0)^2 -- GROMACS funct 1, and biospring_spring_energy in
# forcefield/shared/spring_shared.h -- so there is no factor of two to put
# in.
#
# WHY THE ANGLES ARE CONVERTED HERE WHEN ProteinAtomTorsion.bi.ff LEAVES THEM
# OUT. That file says, correctly, that a 1-3 distance spring is not an angle
# spring, and for AMBER that settles it: the mesh already holds valence
# angles far stiffer than anything a retune would give them. Martini is the
# opposite case. Its angle constants are 20 to 60 kJ.mol-1 and convert to 4.2
# to 18.5 kJ.mol-1.A-2, against the 650 kJ.mol-1.A-2 that -rigidbody defaults
# to -- a factor of 35 to 154. Leaving them at the default does not
# approximate Martini; it replaces a flexible chain with a rigid one. So the
# conversion is not a refinement here, it is the only way this file says
# anything at all.
#
# THE CONVERSION IS DERIVED, AND WHAT IT COSTS IS MEASURED. See
# angle_to_distance in the generator for the derivation, including why the
# sine cancels for GROMACS funct 2 and not for funct 10, and why theta0 = 180
# deg -- arginine's and lysine's BB-SC1-SC2 -- needs no special case even
# though both V''(theta0) and dr13/dtheta vanish there. The cost is listed
# term by term below: the Boltzmann-weighted RMS energy difference between
# Martini's own angle curve and the distance spring, at 300 K, over the range
# the term explores out to 8 kT. It runs from 0.271 to 1.685 kJ.mol-1 over
# the 91 converted records, worst on the backbone BBB angle, which is 0.68 of
# kT. Fitting the constant by least squares instead of matching the curvature
# was measured and rejected: it brings the worst case to 0.668 kJ.mol-1 but
# bakes 300 K into a force-field file and gives up the exact curvature, which
# is what sets the small-amplitude fluctuation.
#
# THE BACKBONE IS THE COIL SET. Martini picks its backbone terms by DSSP and
# BioSpring assigns no secondary structure, so this file carries the
# unconditional link -- bond 0.350 nm at 4000 kJ.mol-1.nm-2, hence 40
# kJ.mol-1.A-2 -- and the coil angle, funct 10 at 127 deg and 20 kJ.mol-1.
# Martini's alternatives, for anyone who wants to edit the generator: helix
# is a 0.310 nm constraint with a funct 2 angle at 96 deg and 700 kJ.mol-1;
# extended is 0.365 nm with funct 2 at 119.2 deg and 150; sheet is funct 10
# at 134 deg and 25, bend 130 and 20, turn 100 and 20.
#
# NOT WRITTEN, each for its own reason. Martini's EQUILIBRIUM LENGTHS: a
# BioSpring spring equilibrates where the input put it, so the lengths in the
# generator serve only to convert the angles. The -scfix terms, angles
# SC1-BB-+BB and BB-+BB-+SC1 at funct 10, 100 deg and 15 kJ.mol-1 plus the
# SC-BB-BB-SC dihedrals at 75 kJ.mol-1: optional in martinize2 and off unless
# -scfix is passed. The elastic bonds BB-++BB and BB-+++BB of extended
# regions (0.640 and 0.970 nm at 2500 kJ.mol-1.nm-2): RigidBodyBuilder moves
# exactly one residue, so those pairs have no spring to retune. The CYS
# SC1->SC1 disulfide constraint at 0.240 nm: use -static-disulfide. And
# everything behind cgidr, with every DSSP-conditional backbone dihedral.
#
# MEASURED CONVERSION ERROR, Boltzmann-weighted RMS energy difference
# from Martini's own angle curve at 300 K, where kT = 2.494 kJ.mol-1.
# One line per angle term, over the residues that carry it:
#
#   Martini angle term                    n  k (kJ.mol-1.A-2)    rms (kJ.mol-1)
#   -BB-BB-+BB funct 10 127.0 deg 20.0 kJ.mol-1   26             8.200             1.685
#   -BB-BB-SC1 funct 2 100.0 deg 25.0 kJ.mol-1   25       4.223-6.389       0.892-0.967
#   SC1-BB-+BB funct 2 100.0 deg 25.0 kJ.mol-1   25       4.223-6.389       0.892-0.967
#   BB-SC1-SC2 funct 2 180.0 deg 25.0 kJ.mol-1    3       8.014-8.433       0.511-0.513
#   BB-SC1-SC2 funct 2 120.0 deg 50.0 kJ.mol-1    4     13.584-13.962             0.360
#   BB-SC1-SC3 funct 2 120.0 deg 50.0 kJ.mol-1    4     13.584-14.945       0.359-0.361
#   BB-SC1-SC2 funct 2 120.0 deg 60.0 kJ.mol-1    2     17.079-18.501             0.326
#   BB-SC1-SC3 funct 2 120.0 deg 60.0 kJ.mol-1    1            18.501             0.326
#   BB-SC1-SC4 funct 2 130.0 deg 60.0 kJ.mol-1    1            15.784             0.271
#
